      "title": "Coverage counts the exclusive session close",
      "description": "`Session.close_utc` is documented in `session_days.py:20` as the first instant after a session, but this join uses inclusive `BETWEEN` on both ends. A trade exactly at `close_ns` is therefore attributed to the session that has already ended, potentially causing a false ledger/raw mismatch or double-counting at a shared boundary. Use a half-open interval (`t.ts_event >= s.open_ns AND t.ts_event < s.close_ns`) and keep the outer scan bound consistent.",
